:227},92,108,[229,230,231,232,233],"Bernabò Brea, Cavalier, 1965, Scavi in Sicilia. Tindari.- Area urbana, L'insula IV e le strade che lo circondano","Boeslager, 1983","Wilson, 1990, Sicily under the Roman Empire: the archaeology of a Roman province, 36 B.C. - A.D. 535","Spigo, 2005, Tindari. L’area archeologica e l’antiquarium","Fasolo, 2013",[235,236,237,238,239],"SFEW4SFD","P9V7GHBT","VF9MMBI9","TC3Z7BBT","X2SEXMRX",[241,242,243,244,27,31,245,246,247,248,246,249,250,141],"isic001904","mosaic depicting wrestlers, with artist's signature",{"_":5},"artist's signature (and labels)","tyndaris","tindari","sicilia","sicily","area archeologica di tindari","ancient greek and latin",[],{"title":253,"body":254,"divs":255,"editions":280,"images":290,"handnote":296},"ISic001904. Mosaic depicting wrestlers, with artist's signature","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy 2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\">  \u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>Verna \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span> Afer \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[ἐπ] ἀγαθῷ \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">Νεικίας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">Διονυσίου\u003C/span>\u003C/span> δοῦλος\u003C/span> · ἐποίει · \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy 2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>VERNA&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;AFER\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[..]ΑΓΑΘΩ\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">ΝΕΙΚΙΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">ΔΙΟΝΥΣΙΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>ΔΟΥΛΟΣ\u003C/span>·ΕΠΟΙΕΙ·\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003Ca href=\"ISic001904_tiled.tif\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic001904_tiled-thumb.tif\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic001904.jpg\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic001904-thumb.jpg\">\u003C/a>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text from autopsy\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"b.1\">b.1: \u003Cspan>Bernabo Brea: ΑΓΑΘΩΝ ΕΙΚΙΑΣ; Guarducci (ap. Boeslager): Νείνας\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Verna, Afer. To good fortune! Neikias, slave of Dionysios made (this).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The labels Verna and Afer can be taken to apply to the two wrestlers. Verna is the formal term for a slave reared as such from birth, while 'Afer' is the ethnic 'African', commonly applied to those from north Africa in the Roman period. Boeslager suggests that this, in context, means a Sicilian competing against an African. The reading of the artist's signature inscription has been somewhat debated, with the transcription of the name Νεικίας causing some initial difficulty (read as Νείνας), or else with the initial N attached to the preceding ΑΓΑΘΩ. it was Guarducci who proposed first that the lacuna at the start should contain ἐπ(ι) and so a traditional wish for good fortune, which in turn frees up the N for the name. (Note that the letters ΕΠ in the final word take up 80mm in width, while being more widely spaced than the letters at the start of the text; and the lacuna at the start of the text is 85mm wide, so the restoration would fit perfectly.) Bilingualism of this sort between content and artist's signature is not uncommon.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bernabò Brea and Cavalier 1965 208 fig.25 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Boeslager 1983 203 no.9 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Wilson 1990 315 fig.268 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Spigo 2005 54 with fig.10 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Fasolo 2013 58 no.4 fig.22 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Tall narrow letters with ovid form to the omicron and theta, with lunate epsilon and sigma and uncial omega. The Latin letters are also relatively tall and narrow, with the top of the A extended.\u003C/p> Line a.1  62-75  Line b.1  92-108  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[256,259,262,265,268,271,274,277],{"id":257,"html":258},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy 2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\">  \u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>Verna \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span> Afer \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[ἐπ] ἀγαθῷ \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">Νεικίας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">Διονυσίου\u003C/span>\u003C/span> δοῦλος\u003C/span> · ἐποίει · \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy 2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>VERNA&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;AFER\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[..]ΑΓΑΘΩ\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">ΝΕΙΚΙΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">ΔΙΟΝΥΣΙΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>ΔΟΥΛΟΣ\u003C/span>·ΕΠΟΙΕΙ·\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":260,"html":261},"facsimile-images","\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003Ca href=\"ISic001904_tiled.tif\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic001904_tiled-thumb.tif\">\u003C/a>\u003Ca href=\"ISic001904.jpg\">\u003Cimg title=\"I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\" src=\"ISic001904-thumb.jpg\">\u003C/a>",{"id":263,"html":264},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text from autopsy\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"b.1\">b.1: \u003Cspan>Bernabo Brea: ΑΓΑΘΩΝ ΕΙΚΙΑΣ; Guarducci (ap. Boeslager): Νείνας\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":266,"html":267},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Verna, Afer. To good fortune! Neikias, slave of Dionysios made (this).\u003C/p>  ",{"id":269,"html":270},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The labels Verna and Afer can be taken to apply to the two wrestlers. Verna is the formal term for a slave reared as such from birth, while 'Afer' is the ethnic 'African', commonly applied to those from north Africa in the Roman period. Boeslager suggests that this, in context, means a Sicilian competing against an African. The reading of the artist's signature inscription has been somewhat debated, with the transcription of the name Νεικίας causing some initial difficulty (read as Νείνας), or else with the initial N attached to the preceding ΑΓΑΘΩ. it was Guarducci who proposed first that the lacuna at the start should contain ἐπ(ι) and so a traditional wish for good fortune, which in turn frees up the N for the name. (Note that the letters ΕΠ in the final word take up 80mm in width, while being more widely spaced than the letters at the start of the text; and the lacuna at the start of the text is 85mm wide, so the restoration would fit perfectly.) Bilingualism of this sort between content and artist's signature is not uncommon.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":272,"html":273},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bernabò Brea and Cavalier 1965 208 fig.25 \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Boeslager 1983 203 no.9 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Wilson 1990 315 fig.268 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Spigo 2005 54 with fig.10 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Fasolo 2013 58 no.4 fig.22 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  ",{"id":275,"html":276},"handnote","\u003Cp>Tall narrow letters with ovid form to the omicron and theta, with lunate epsilon and sigma and uncial omega. The Latin letters are also relatively tall and narrow, with the top of the A extended.\u003C/p> Line a.1  62-75  Line b.1  92-108  Interlineation line 1 to 2    ",{"id":278,"html":279},"license"," Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. ",[281,283,286,287],{"html":282},"Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: autopsy 2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site",{"id":284,"html":285},"edition-interpretive","\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>Verna \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.)\u003C/span> Afer \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[ἐπ] ἀγαθῷ \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">Νεικίας\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">Διονυσίου\u003C/span>\u003C/span> δοῦλος\u003C/span> · ἐποίει · \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"html":282},{"id":288,"html":289},"edition-diplomatic","\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"aba\">section a\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"diva--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"aa-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>VERNA&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;AFER\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cspan class=\"textpartnumber\" id=\"abb\">section b\u003C/span>\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"divb--diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"ab-l1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[..]ΑΓΑΘΩ\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Νεικίας Διονυσίου δοῦλος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Νεικίας\">ΝΕΙΚΙΑΣ\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Διονυσίου\">ΔΙΟΝΥΣΙΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>ΔΟΥΛΟΣ\u003C/span>·ΕΠΟΙΕΙ·\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",[291,293],{"image":115,"thumb":292,"title":118},"ISic001904_tiled-thumb.tif",{"image":294,"thumb":295,"title":118},"ISic001904.jpg","ISic001904-thumb.jpg",[297],{"html":58},"\u003C?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"https://epidoc.stoa.org/schema/latest/tei-epidoc.rng\" type=\"application/xml\" schematypens=\"http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0\"?>\n\u003C?xml-model href=\"../schematron/ircyr-checking.sch\" schematypens=\"http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron\"?>\n\u003CTEI xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:xi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude\" xml:lang=\"en\">\n    \u003CteiHeader>\n        \u003CfileDesc>\n            \u003CtitleStmt>\n                \u003Ctitle>Mosaic depicting wrestlers, with artist's signature\u003C/title>\n                \u003Ceditor ref=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/editor>\n                \u003Cprincipal ref=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/principal>\n                \u003Cfunder>John Fell OUP Research Fund\u003C/funder>\n\t   \u003Cfunder>\u003Cref target=\"https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/885040\">ERC Advanced Grant no.885040\u003C/ref>\u003C/funder>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"JP\" ref=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>original data collection and editing\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n                \u003CrespStmt>\n                    \u003Cname xml:id=\"AA\" ref=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703\">Alex Antoniou\u003C/name>\n                    \u003Cresp>autopsy participation\u003C/resp>\n                \u003C/respStmt>\n          \u003CrespStmt>\u003Cname xml:id=\"Coccato\" ref=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6641-2820\">Alessia Coccato\u003C/name>\u003Cresp>Petrographic observation and analysis\u003C/resp>\u003C/respStmt>\n            \u003C/titleStmt>\n            \u003CpublicationStmt>\n                \u003Cauthority>I.Sicily\u003C/authority>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"filename\">ISic001904\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"TM\">698370\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDR\">150007\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDH\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"EDCS\">70901006\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"PHI\"/>\n                \u003Cidno type=\"URI\">http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001904\u003C/idno>\n                \u003Cavailability>\n                    \u003Clicence target=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.\u003C/licence>\n                \u003C/availability>\n            \u003C/publicationStmt>\n            \u003CsourceDesc>\n                \u003CmsDesc>\n                    \u003CmsIdentifier>\n                        \u003Ccountry>Italy\u003C/country>\n                        \u003Cregion>Sicily\u003C/region>\n                        \u003Csettlement>Tindari\u003C/settlement>\n                        \u003Crepository role=\"site\" ref=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/189\">Area archeologica di Tindari\u003C/repository>\n                       \u003CaltIdentifier>\n                            \u003Csettlement>\u003C/settlement>\n                            \u003Crepository>\u003C/repository>\n                           \u003Cidno>\u003C/idno>\n                        \u003C/altIdentifier>\n                    \u003C/msIdentifier>\n                    \u003CmsContents>\n                        \u003CtextLang mainLang=\"grc\" otherLangs=\"la\">Ancient Greek and Latin\u003C/textLang>\n                    \u003C/msContents>\n                    \u003CphysDesc>\n                        \u003CobjectDesc>\n                            \u003CsupportDesc>\n                                \u003Csupport>\u003Cp>A mosaic 'doormat' at the entrance to the frigidarium of the insula IV baths at Tindari. A Greek inscription runs along the lower edge, above which is a rectangular black border surrounding a white field, on which are depicted in black tesserae two naked figures facing one another in a fighting stance, and behind each is depicted a large krater, a palm branch, and a victor's wreath, with a Latin label behind each figure's head. The lower left corner is lost and some of the tesserae of the Greek text are missing. The section containing the Greek text is 119 cm wide (originally 127.5) and 12-13 cm high.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.inorganic.stone.mosaic\" type=\"stone.mosaic\" subtype=\"unspecified\" resp=\"#Coccato\">mosaic\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.pavement\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/190.html\">pavement\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">81\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\">143\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\">\u003C/depth>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.damaged\"/>\n\t\t    \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\u003Cp>A single line of Greek along the lower edge, and two Latin labels in the main pictorial field.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.mosaic\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/16\">mosaic\u003C/rs>\n                                \t\u003Cdamage ana=\"#text_condition.deteriorated\"/>\n\t\t\t\u003C/layout>\n                            \u003C/layoutDesc>\n                        \u003C/objectDesc>\n                        \u003ChandDesc>\n                            \u003ChandNote>\u003Cp>Tall narrow letters with ovid form to the omicron and theta, with lunate epsilon and sigma and uncial omega. The Latin letters are also relatively tall and narrow, with the top of the A extended.\u003C/p>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"linea.1\" to=\"linea.1\">Line a.1\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"62\" atMost=\"75\">62-75\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"lineb.1\" to=\"lineb.1\">Line b.1\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"letterHeight\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\" atLeast=\"92\" atMost=\"108\">92-108\u003C/height>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003Clocus from=\"line1\" to=\"line2\">Interlineation line 1 to 2\u003C/locus>\n                                \u003Cdimensions type=\"interlinear\">\n                                    \u003Cheight unit=\"mm\"/>\n                                \u003C/dimensions>\n                            \u003C/handNote>\n                        \u003C/handDesc>\n                    \u003C/physDesc>\n                    \u003Chistory>\n                        \u003Corigin>\n                            \u003CorigPlace>\u003Cregion>Sicilia\u003C/region>\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"ancient\" ref=\"http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462527\">Tyndaris\u003C/placeName>\t\t\n                                \u003CplaceName type=\"modern\" ref=\"http://sws.geonames.org/10282151\">Tindari\u003C/placeName>\n                            \t\u003Cgeo>38.14227, 15.04385\u003C/geo>\n\t\t\u003C/origPlace>\n                            \u003CorigDate datingMethod=\"#julian\" notBefore-custom=\"0151\" notAfter-custom=\"0250\" evidence=\"lettering archaeological-context\">later second or earlier third century CE\u003C/origDate>\n                        \u003C/origin>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"found\" subtype=\"discovered\">In situ at the entrance to the frigidarium on the north side of the peristyle of the house at the northern end of insula IV, Tindari\u003Cgeo>38.1432591,15.0430593\u003C/geo>\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003Cprovenance type=\"observed\" subtype=\"autopsied\" resp=\"#JP #AA\" xml:id=\"autopsy\">2022-07-14 Prag and Antoniou, on site\u003C/provenance>\n                        \u003Cacquisition/>\n                    \u003C/history>\n                \u003C/msDesc>\n            \u003C/sourceDesc>\n        \u003C/fileDesc>\n        \u003CencodingDesc>\n             \u003Cp>Encoded following the latest EpiDoc guidelines\u003C/p>\n             \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/ISicily-taxonomies.xml\">\n                 \u003Cxi:fallback>\n                     \u003Cp>Taxonomies for ISicily controlled values\u003C/p>\n                 \u003C/xi:fallback>\n             \u003C/xi:include>\n\t  \u003Cxi:include href=\"../alists/charDecl.xml\">\n\t     \u003Cxi:fallback>\n\t       \u003Cp>ISicily glyphs authority list\u003C/p>\n\t     \u003C/xi:fallback>\n\t   \u003C/xi:include>\n         \u003C/encodingDesc>\n        \u003CprofileDesc>\n            \u003CcalendarDesc>\n                \u003Ccalendar xml:id=\"julian\">\n                    \u003Cp>Julian Calendar\u003C/p>\n                \u003C/calendar>\n            \u003C/calendarDesc>\n            \u003ClangUsage>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"en\">English\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"it\">Italian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"grc\">Ancient Greek\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"la\">Latin\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"he\">Hebrew\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"phn\">Phoenician\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xpu\">Punic\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"osc\">Oscan\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"xly\">Elymian\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"scx\">Sikel\u003C/language>\n                \u003Clanguage ident=\"sxc\">Sikan\u003C/language>\n            \u003C/langUsage>\n            \u003CtextClass>\n                \u003Ckeywords scheme=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription\">\n                    \u003Cterm ana=\"#function.attribution.production.artist\" ref=\"https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Artist\">Artist's signature (and labels)\u003C/term>\n                \u003C/keywords>\n            \u003C/textClass>\n        \u003C/profileDesc>\n        \u003CrevisionDesc status=\"edited\">\n            \u003ClistChange>\n                        \u003Cchange when=\"2026-06-03\" who=\"#JP\">Jonathan Prag created from autopsy and photographs\u003C/change>\n\t\u003C/listChange>\n        \u003C/revisionDesc>\n    \u003C/teiHeader>\n    \u003Cfacsimile>\n        \u003Csurface type=\"front\">\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"screen\" url=\"ISic001904_tiled.tif\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n            \u003Cgraphic n=\"print\" url=\"ISic001904.jpg\" height=\"3680px\" width=\"5520px\">\n                \u003Cdesc>I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2022-07-14\u003C/desc>\n            \u003C/graphic>\n         \u003C/surface>\n        \u003C/facsimile>\n    \u003Ctext>\n        \u003Cbody>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"edition\" subtype=\"primary\" xml:space=\"preserve\" resp=\"#JP\" source=\"#autopsy\">\n                \u003Cdiv type=\"textpart\" subtype=\"section\" n=\"a\" xml:lang=\"la\">\n                    \u003Cab>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"1\"/>Verna \u003Cspace unit=\"character\" extent=\"unknown\"/> Afer\n                    \u003C/ab>\n                \u003C/div>\n                \u003Cdiv type=\"textpart\" subtype=\"section\" n=\"b\" xml:lang=\"grc\">\n                    \u003Cab>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"1\"/>\u003Csupplied reason=\"lost\">ἐπ\u003C/supplied> ἀγαθῷ \u003CpersName type=\"attested\">\u003Cname>Νεικίας\u003C/name> \u003CpersName type=\"attested\">\u003Cname>Διονυσίου\u003C/name>\u003C/persName> δοῦλος\u003C/persName> \u003Cg ref=\"#interpunct\">·\u003C/g> ἐποίει \u003Cg ref=\"#interpunct\">·\u003C/g>\n                    \u003C/ab>\n                \u003C/div>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"apparatus\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003ClistApp>\n                    \u003Capp>\u003Cnote>Text from autopsy\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                    \u003Capp loc=\"b.1\">\u003Cnote>Bernabo Brea: ΑΓΑΘΩΝ ΕΙΚΙΑΣ; Guarducci (ap. Boeslager): Νείνας\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\n                \u003C/listApp>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"translation\" xml:lang=\"en\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cp>Verna, Afer. To good fortune! Neikias, slave of Dionysios made (this).\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"commentary\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cp>The labels Verna and Afer can be taken to apply to the two wrestlers. Verna is the formal term for a slave reared as such from birth, while 'Afer' is the ethnic 'African', commonly applied to those from north Africa in the Roman period. Boeslager suggests that this, in context, means a Sicilian competing against an African. The reading of the artist's signature inscription has been somewhat debated, with the transcription of the name Νεικίας causing some initial difficulty (read as Νείνας), or else with the initial N attached to the preceding ΑΓΑΘΩ. it was Guarducci who proposed first that the lacuna at the start should contain ἐπ(ι) and so a traditional wish for good fortune, which in turn frees up the N for the name. (Note that the letters ΕΠ in the final word take up 80mm in width, while being more widely spaced than the letters at the start of the text; and the lacuna at the start of the text is 85mm wide, so the restoration would fit perfectly.) Bilingualism of this sort between content and artist's signature is not uncommon.\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"bibliography\">\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"edition\">\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Bernabò Brea and Cavalier\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1965\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>208 fig.25\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/SFEW4SFD\"/>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Boeslager\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1983\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>203 no.9\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/P9V7GHBT\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002610\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Wilson\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>1990\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>315 fig.268\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/VF9MMBI9\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001509\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                    \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Spigo\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>2005\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>54 with fig.10\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/TC3Z7BBT\"/>\n                        \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001569\u003C/ref>\n                    \u003C/bibl>\n                  \u003Cbibl>\n                        \u003Cauthor>Fasolo\u003C/author>\n                        \u003Cdate>2013\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>58 no.4 fig.22\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/X2SEXMRX\"/>\n                    \u003Cref target=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002011\u003C/ref>\n                  \u003C/bibl>\n                \u003C/listBibl>\n\t   \u003ClistBibl type=\"discussion\">\u003Cbibl/>\u003C/listBibl>\n            \u003C/div>\n        \u003C/body>\n    \u003C/text>\n\u003C/TEI>\n"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
